    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0212" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/14863</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Captain Roscoe E. Schuirmann of the Office
                        of the Chief of Naval Operations</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-10">July 10, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following information has been received from Naval Attaché Chungking— It is
                    reported that the brother of the Governor of Sinkiang who recently visited
                    Chungking and negotiated with Chiang Kai-shek was assassinated at Urumchi on
                    July 5th. If this is true it may indicate a serious setback to recently improved
                        relations.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d173-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuirmann</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d173-f1" n="17" xml:id="d173-f1-content">
                <p>Marginal notation by the Adviser on Political Relations (Hornbeck): “And it <hi
                        rendition="#italic">might</hi> indicate any one of several other things. S.
                    K. H.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
